 expectations:\n- 2.675 -> 2.68\n- 2.665 -> 2.66\n\nCI: passed on 08d3cd5986 (ci-0001 status and ci-0002).\n\nNote: ci-0001's wait_for_ci output referenced main@0c0ffee000 and a flaky tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals failure; the branch-specific status and a re-run on the branch commit both passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-pr-fix-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex requested for review.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` per FIN-212, which is what the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` expect (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66).\n- **Branch:** `fix/fin-212-half-even-rounding`, commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** The first run (`ci-0001`) returned conflicting output. Its status endpoint and the branch run list showed `passed` for `08d3cd5986`, but `wait_for_ci` reported a failure on `main@0c0ffee000` in a flaky `test_ledger.py::test_totals`. I triggered a second run on the same commit (`ci-0002`), which passed. The PR description notes the discrepancy.\n- **PR:** #101, `fix/fin-212-half-even-rounding` into `main`, reviewer alex. I did not merge it. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\nThe mismatched output from `ci-0001` is unexplained, so it may be worth checking why the CI system reported a main SHA for a branch run.", "type": "text"}]}]}